{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2535 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fd6f0940d289ca2e7f51e74942a626e6b709fb6394d6edb93a43c81873d216f5" :edb/db-before-t 2534 :edb/db-after-t 2535 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535847 50 #inst "2026-10-09T08:51:57.405Z" 13194139535847 true] [17592186119683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369947 13194139535847 true] [17592186119683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369954 13194139535847 true] [17592186119683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369961 13194139535847 true] [17592186119684 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369933 13194139535847 true] [17592186119684 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369940 13194139535847 true] [17592186369933 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369934 13194139535847 true] [17592186369933 1089 "q-132125" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369933 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535847 true] [17592186369933 1100 "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=0$ for the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩.$" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369933 1113 #uuid "6760ac8d-6b9d-57a0-830e-36a645310793" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369933 1145 "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-{e}^{-t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨1,\\,-{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(0)$ and ${r}^{″}(0)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})^{3}}{1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369935 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369936 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369937 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369938 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369939 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1041 "selection" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369938 13194139535847 true] [17592186369934 1110 #uuid "a39f22d2-09d6-5ba2-b65e-57d3438ae6e9" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369935 1034 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369935 1111 #uuid "a2dbdd45-cc28-5675-9466-5c39a85615ab" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369936 1034 "2" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369936 1111 #uuid "ba6b8384-d8db-5e10-a3c0-f45c29f6d903" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369937 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369937 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369937 1111 #uuid "33a848c4-124c-5c97-a276-b2b3c10ef78b" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369938 1034 "2\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369938 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369938 1111 #uuid "af59fb76-438f-5a8b-a629-65029671bc95" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369939 1034 "4" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369939 1111 #uuid "9c3a7380-8a7b-5249-b9e9-f762c93c0c75" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369940 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369941 13194139535847 true] [17592186369940 1089 "q-132129" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369940 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535847 true] [17592186369940 1100 "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=\\pi $ for the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369940 1113 #uuid "a402dcc4-c7d6-5188-8327-7ca541f9ca6f" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369940 1145 "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(\\pi ),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & ={e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-t}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi )$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\times 2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨0,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{({e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{2})^{3}}{2{e}^{-2\\pi }} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-3\\pi }}{2{e}^{-2\\pi }} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369942 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369943 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369944 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369945 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369946 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1041 "selection" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369945 13194139535847 true] [17592186369941 1110 #uuid "3e95326b-1972-509c-bd41-38bbe4ef360d" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369942 1034 "2{e}^{\\pi }" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369942 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369942 1111 #uuid "5e16b62f-5545-5fba-822b-7bd4263b310e" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369943 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi }}{2}" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369943 1111 #uuid "b97da160-c3cb-56c6-8ca1-52543b94f7f2" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369944 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{2}" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369944 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369944 1111 #uuid "fac2f82e-26a4-59c0-9b00-4f8c2d5a9620" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369945 1034 "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\pi }" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369945 1111 #uuid "eab75d75-e963-598a-8849-7c24495fecdf" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369946 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{2}" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369946 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535847 true] [17592186369946 1111 #uuid "0118fbaa-d4cf-5fab-a532-5966df9538f9" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369947 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369948 13194139535847 true] [17592186369947 1089 "q-132194" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369947 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535847 true] [17592186369947 1100 "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(1,-1)$ where $t=1,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖=\\sqrt{13},$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}},\\,-\\frac{3t}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}⟩.\n$$" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369947 1113 #uuid "45bddeff-8807-5684-8070-dc3abab32e36" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369947 1145 "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(1)=⟨1,-1⟩,$ since the point $P(1,-1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(1)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(1)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3t}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{18t}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}},\\,-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}}⟨-3t,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{(9({1}^{2})+4)}^{3}}}⟨-3(1),-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot \\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot \\sqrt{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{(\\frac{6}{13})} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=1$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1)+R(1)N(1) & =⟨1,-1⟩+\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1⟩+\\frac{13}{6}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1⟩+⟨-\\frac{13}{2},-\\frac{13}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{11}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369949 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369950 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369951 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369952 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369953 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1041 "selection" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369949 13194139535847 true] [17592186369948 1110 #uuid "9c7b6cb4-3e04-5b4c-825c-3eb818e4f343" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369949 1034 "The center is $⟨-\\frac{11}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}$" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535847 true] [17592186369949 1111 #uuid "d4b9007a-f91c-5fab-8