{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨0,1⟩,$ since the point $P(0,1)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨0,1⟩+\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩+⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369956 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369957 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369958 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369959 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369960 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1041 "selection" 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369958 13194139535847 true] [17592186369955 1110 #uuid "e7107b47-8e6a-5848-98c5-ea5b10956e86" 13